For a larger display, Adrian doubles both the height and width of the entire grid. Calculate the number of square inches in the area of Adrian's original kite.

In the rectangular coordinate system $(xOy)$, the curve $C\_1$: $x+y=1$ and the curve $C\_2$: $\begin{cases} x=2+2\cos\varphi \ y=2\sin\varphi \end{cases} (\varphi\in[0,2\pi))$ are given. Establish a polar coordinate system with the coordinate origin $O$ as the pole and the non-negative semi-axis of the $x$-axis as the polar axis.

(I) Write the polar equations of the curves $C\_1$ and $C\_2$;

(II) In the polar coordinate system, point $A$ is the common point of ray $l$: $\theta=\alpha (\rho\geqslant 0)$ and $C\_1$, point $B$ is the common point of $l$ and $C\_2$. Find the maximum value of $\frac{|OB|}{|OA|}$ as $\alpha$ varies in the interval $\left[0, \frac{\pi}{2}\right]$.

